    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d480">

                <pb facs="1220" n="1189" xml:id="pg1189"/>

                <head>480. Note From President Carter to Secretary of State Vance and the
                    President’s Assistant for National Security Affairs (Brzezinski)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d480-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1978-02-27">February 27, 1978</date>
                    </dateline></opener>
                <opener>
                    <salute>Cy &amp; Zbig</salute>
                </opener>
                <p>We need to evolve soon US position re UN Disarmament Conference. We’re in danger
                    of being clobbered by all nations for arms sales &amp; by Soviets on ER
                    weapons.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#bold">J.C.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d480-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d480-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Executive Secretariat Files, Lot 84D161, Box 1,
                    Miscellaneous. No classification marking. Carter hand-wrote the note. Brzezinski
                    forwarded the note under cover of a February 27 memorandum. (Ibid.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
